Do bosun first, then hull; each is its own PR and each is R-gov (`.bosun/**`, `.claude/**`, `.splice/**`), so the owner approves each head as in F. A repo set up with bosun init or hull has .splice/channels/bosun.toml and cannot run bosun pin (it refuses, exit 1): there splice update --all below also updates the bosun channel (or splice update --channel bosun alone), so skip the bosun pin lines and the npm line; install the bosun version the merged channel update put in .bosun/version. The bosun pin lines are for a repo set up with bosun adopt. Cloud sessions run the repo's own setup script, whose tool pins come with the bosun release: bosun 0.18.0's script pins splice 0.6.0, hoist 0.5.1 and berth 0.2.1, so a cloud session runs those until a later bosun release moves them. Merge only when ci-ok is green. Both paths in full: [Update](/docs/update/).
